  "emailBody": "\n        <html>\n\n        <body\n            style=\"\n                font-family:Segoe UI, Arial, sans-serif;\n                margin:20px;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    background:#d42e12;\n                    color:white;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                \"\n            >\n\n\n               <h1 style=\"margin:0;\">\n                    Fuel Market Intelligence Morning Report\n                </h1>\n\n                <p style=\"margin:5px 0 0 0;\">\n                    20 August 2026\n                </p>\n\n            </div>\n\n            <p\n                style=\"\n                    font-size:16px;\n                    margin-top:20px;\n                    margin-bottom:20px;\n                \"\n            >\n                Good morning Sir,\n                <br><br>\n                \n                Here is today's fuel market intelligence report highlighting\n                the latest PMS and AGO depot prices together with key industry\n                developments and market news.\n            </p>\n\n            <br>\n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            PMS Prices\n        </h2>\n\n        <div\n            style=\"\n                background:#fad5a1;\n                padding:12px;\n                border-left:5px solid #f28e05;\n                margin-bottom:10px;\n                font-size:16px;\n                font-weight:bold;\n            \"\n        >\n            Average PMS Prices: ₦1,185.12/L\n        </div>\n\n        <table\n            width=\"100%\"\n            cellspacing=\"0\"\n            cellpadding=\"10\"\n            style=\"\n                border-collapse:collapse;\n                border:1px solid #ddd;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <tr style=\"background:#d42e12;color:white;\">\n                <th align=\"left\">Depot</th>\n                <th align=\"left\">Price</th>\n            </tr>\n\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AFRICAN TERMINAL</td>\n                <td>₦1,195.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>INTERGRATED</td>\n                <td>₦1,195.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>LIQUID BULK</td>\n                <td>₦1,185.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>TSL</td>\n                <td>₦1,185.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>SIGMUND</td>\n                <td>₦1,185.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>PINNACLE</td>\n                <td>₦1,170.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DANGOTE</td>\n                <td>₦1,168.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>NIPCO LAGOS</td>\n                <td>₦1,198.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            AGO Prices\n        </h2>\n\n        <div\n            style=\"\n                background:#fad5a1;\n                padding:12px;\n                border-left:5px solid #f28e05;\n                margin-bottom:10px;\n                font-size:16px;\n                font-weight:bold;\n            \"\n        >\n            Average AGO Prices: ₦1,659.25/L\n        </div>\n\n        <table\n            width=\"100%\"\n            cellspacing=\"0\"\n            cellpadding=\"10\"\n            style=\"\n                border-collapse:collapse;\n                border:1px solid #ddd;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <tr style=\"background:#d42e12;color:white;\">\n                <th align=\"left\">Depot</th>\n                <th align=\"left\">Price</th>\n            </tr>\n\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DUPORT</td>\n                <td>₦1,660.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBETO</td>\n                <td>₦1,660.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AFRICAN TERMINAL</td>\n                <td>₦1,664.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>INTERGRATED</td>\n                <td>₦1,660.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>GULF TREASURE</td>\n                <td>₦1,660.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>TMDK</td>\n                <td>₦1,660.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>OBAT OIL</td>\n                <td>₦1,655.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBACHEM</td>\n                <td>₦1,655.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            Market News\n        </h2>\n        \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Subsidy, ₦200/Litre Petrol Price Would Have Crushed Dangote Refinery — FG\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The Federal Government has said that the Dangote Petroleum Refinery could not have operated commercially under Nigeria’s former petrol subsidy regime. The Minister of Finance and Coordinating Minister of the Economy, Taiwo Oyedele, stated this in Abuja. He said the removal of the petrol subsidy, alongside the unification of the foreign exchange market, came with significant costs.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/subsidy-200litre-petrol-price-would-have-crushed-dangote-refinery-fg\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    FG: No 'Subsidy Savings' Line Exists as ₦15.8trn Already Outspent — Oyedele\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Nigeria's Federal Government has clarified that the ₦15.8 trillion in resources mobilised from subsidy removal and foreign exchange reforms did not translate into a pool of unspent cash. Finance Minister and Coordinating Minister of the Economy, Taiwo Oyedele, disclosed this while presenting the government's Reform Scorecard.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/fg-no-subsidy-savings-line-exists-as-158trn-already-outspent-oyedele\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    EFCC Recovers ₦4.5bn Diesel From Ibafon Depot as Prudent Energy Alleges Diversion\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The Economic and Financial Crimes Commission (EFCC) has recovered 2.3 million litres of Automotive Gas Oil (AGO), commonly known as diesel, from Ibafon Oil and Gas in Lagos. The recovery was carried out on Monday, August 17, 2026, by the EFCC’s Lagos Zonal Directorate 1 after a petition by Prudent Energy and Services Limited. The commission said the outstanding stock was initially recorded at 2,574,031 litres following periodic withdrawals.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/efcc-recovers-45bn-diesel-from-ibafon-depot-as-prudent-energy-alleges-diversion\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Diesel Landing Cost Hits ₦1,709 as Dangote Refinery Holds at ₦1,570/Litre\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Nigeria’s estimated spot landing cost for Automotive Gas Oil (AGO), commonly known as diesel, has climbed to ₦1,709.60 per litre. The price gap has coincided with increased truck activity around Dangote Refinery. The lower refinery-gate price gives buyers an incentive to source AGO locally.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/diesel-landing-cost-hits-1709-as-dangote-refinery-holds-at-1570litre\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Truck Traffic Returns to Dangote Refinery as Lower Gantry Prices Attract Buyers\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Heavy truck traffic has returned to the Dangote Petroleum Refinery as marketers increase purchases of petrol and diesel. The renewed activity has been particularly visible in diesel, with trucks lining up to load from the refinery as marketers take advantage of the widening price gap.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/truck-traffic-returns-to-dangote-refinery-as-lower-gantry-prices-attract-buyers\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
